          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: The witness in 2008 recounted an observation made during the summer between 1990 and 1993 (the date of 01/06/1990 is given arbitrarily). One evening around 11 PM, while preparing to camp with a friend in his backyard, the witness, aged around ten, observed from his tent's entrance the arrival in the clear sky of three white lights forming an opaque triangular shape of great size. The phenomenon moved silently and very slowly above the town on a straight trajectory. During the brief observation, the witness had the impression that the main triangle was formed by a set of triangles due to other lights. The young boy was frightened, and his friend did not have time to see the phenomenon. Only one testimony was collected. This testimony is not exploitable by GEIPAN because it is an observation made by a child reported 18 years after the facts, without specifying the date (nor even the year) of the observation. GEIPAN is not even able to search its database and make comparisons with nearby testimonies in terms of location and/or date. Consequently, GEIPAN classifies this case as C: lack of information.",
